@suite:frontend-fsharp @refusal @basis:hand-authored
Feature: Refuse attributes with an effect, type tests and casts
  Morphir has no runtime types and no subtyping, and an attribute must not
  change the meaning of the code. See the fsharp-source-frontend spec and the
  rule catalog.

  Scenario Outline: frontend-fsharp-0060 An attribute with an effect has a precise refusal
    Given the F# package "acme/demo" exposing "Pricing"
    And the source "Pricing.fs":
      """fsharp
      namespace Acme.Demo
      module Pricing =
          [<Literal>]
          let MaxDays = 30
      """
    When it is compiled from <input> with IR version <version>
    Then compilation fails with diagnostics:
      """json
      [{"severity":"error","code":"fsharp.unsupported_attribute","location":{"uri":"Pricing.fs","range":{"start":{"line":2,"character":6},"end":{"line":2,"character":13}}}}]
      """

    Examples:
      | input        | version |
      | files        | 1       |
      | files        | 2       |
      | files        | 3       |
      | files        | 4       |
      | directory    | 1       |
      | directory    | 2       |
      | directory    | 3       |
      | directory    | 4       |
      | project file | 1       |
      | project file | 2       |
      | project file | 3       |
      | project file | 4       |

